Upstream: https://github.com/IBM/plex  (also served by Google Fonts)

Files, taken from Google Fonts' latin subsets and byte-identical to them:

  plex-sans-var-latin.woff2   IBM Plex Sans, variable weight 400-700, latin subset
                              https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/ibmplexsans/v23/zYXzKVElMYYaJe8bpLHnCwDKr932-G7dytD-Dmu1syxeKYbSB4Zh.woff2
  plex-cond-600-latin.woff2   IBM Plex Sans Condensed 600, latin subset
                              https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/ibmplexsanscondensed/v15/Gg8gN4UfRSqiPg7Jn2ZI12V4DCEwkj1E4LVeHY527LvspYYnFBq4.woff2
  plex-cond-700-latin.woff2   IBM Plex Sans Condensed 700, latin subset
                              https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/ibmplexsanscondensed/v15/Gg8gN4UfRSqiPg7Jn2ZI12V4DCEwkj1E4LVeHY4S7bvspYYnFBq4.woff2

Self-hosted on purpose: a font fetched from a CDN is a font that is not there when the boat is offshore,
and this app has to render the same tied up as it does ten miles out. They are in the service worker's
precache list and inlined as data URIs in the single-file build.

Latin only. If you adapt Saily to a passage whose names need more, take the fuller subsets from upstream.
